# fixedbugs, defect 2464 (panel 245's R1, provisional), 2026-11-11.
#
# SYMPTOM: a door of the program's own header shifting an `int` by 40 built
# at exit 0, clang's `shift count >= width of type [-Wshift-count-overflow]`
# printed raw, and the program printed `2` (measured at batch 31's base,
# 9febdd6c3), what the machine gave: a header's code was held to a list of
# what stays an error, and a word of undefined behaviour outside it was a
# warning.
#
# FIX: a header's own code fails closed: every warning clang gives there is
# an error but `-Wall`'s, sign conversions and deprecations, a `#warning` and
# a `#pragma message` told and never refused (`emit/header_region.hero`'s
# `LINE_WORDS`), so the header is refused at its line, at exit 1.

extern "fixedbugs-2464-a-header-s-own-shift-past-its-width-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function door(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(door(x: 1))
